NXR-157|Optional host memory analysis and fail-closed symbol audits|Verification|Native C++ host fixtures shall support optional ASan/UBSan and separate Valgrind Memcheck execution; firmware name audits shall reject empty or stripped symbol evidence and bound compiler/audit subprocesses.|Static analysis and target symbol checks do not expose all host memory defects, while absent symbols cannot support a name-based no-heap claim.|Separate presets instrument native C++ or add finite Memcheck variants; both reject firmware configurations; stripped compiler fixture and symbol-presence self-tests pass; tool subprocess failures remain failures.|Actual sanitizer/Memcheck CTest and ARM/RV32 compiler contracts.|NXR-085,NXR-152,NXR-156|CMake native checks and XDoc C# bounded executor; no custom Python tooling.|No target heap, RAM fields or runtime instrumentation; host model results do not qualify firmware.|cmake/host-memory.cmake,cmake/host-tests.cmake,tools/Rtos.Tools/Program.cs,tools/HostProcess.cs,docs/host-memory.rst|Known-symbol audit remains a limited check against recognizable allocation paths, not proof against arbitrary renamed/custom allocators.|cmake/host-memory.cmake,cmake/host-tests.cmake,tools/Rtos.Tools/Program.cs,tools/HostProcess.cs|tools/Rtos.Tools/Program.cs,tests/ipc_random.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
